 `hermes config check` reports sections missing from an older config.
 
+### Timezone, Location, Weather & File Activity (self-settable)
+
+`timezone`, `location`, `weather`, and `file_activity` are injected as
+ambient context on every turn (a `Current time: ...` line, a `Location: ...`
+line, a `Weather: ...` line, and a `Last edited: ...` line on the API copy of
+the user message — never in the cached system prompt). The agent sees them
+without the user having to repeat where/when they are or what they were doing.
+Weather uses Open-Meteo (free, no API key) and is cached for ~20 minutes. File
+activity scans the working directory for recently modified files (skipping
+`.git`, `node_modules`, `venv`, `__pycache__`, etc.) and is cached for ~5
+minutes.
+
+**You can set these yourself** when the user tells you where they are or you
+infer a timezone mismatch — run `hermes config set location "Riverton"` or
+`hermes config set timezone  "Region/X"`. The location and weather
+take effect on the very next turn (re-resolved each turn); timezone may need
+a `/reset` in a long-lived CLI session (cached at first use). Don't ask the
+user to run the command — just run it and confirm.
+
+Disable weather with `hermes config set weather.enabled false` (e.g. if the
+user is on a metered connection or doesn't want the network call). Disable
+file activity with `hermes config set file_activity.enabled false`.
+
 ### Toolsets
 
 Enable/disable via `hermes tools` (interactive) or `hermes tools enable/disable NAME`.
